# Builder.io — Fieldnote space, main environment
NEXT_PUBLIC_BUILDER_API_KEY=3a593c5220b04d469e25606e2987ebc0

# Cloudinary — the secondary DAM this app coexists with (see
# src/lib/cloudinary/builder-plugin.tsx for the full pattern writeup).
#
# CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME is a public identifier, the same way Builder's own
# API key above is public — it's meant to appear in client-side widget
# config and in URLs (Cloudinary's own docs embed it in every asset URL:
# https://res.cloudinary.com/<cloud_name>/...). Safe to expose in the
# browser bundle.
#
# CLOUDINARY_API_KEY and CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET are NOT safe to expose.
# They're used only server-side, in scripts/setup-cloudinary.ts (via
# src/lib/cloudinary/ensure-upload-preset.ts) to manage the account's
# upload presets through Cloudinary's Admin API. The in-editor image picker
# itself never uses these two — it authenticates uploads with the unsigned
# preset name instead (see the "signed vs unsigned uploads" comment in
# ensure-upload-preset.ts), which is what makes it safe to run entirely in
# the browser with zero secrets in the client bundle. Never commit real
# values for these two, and never let either reach client-side code or a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_-prefixed variable.
CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=
